---
title: Mom’s chicken bow ties
servings: 4
source: Hometown Cooking from Better Homes and Gardens, February 2002
image: https://tastefullygrace.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Sun-Dried-Tomato-Pasta-Recipe-1-500x500.jpg
---
Cook @bow tie pasta{227%g} according to package directions; drain. Meanwhile, in a large skillet, cook the @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) in hot @olive oil{2%tbsp} over medium-high heat for ~{30%seconds}.

Add @boneless, skinless chicken breast{1%lb}(cut into thin bite-sized strips), @dried basil{1%tsp}, and @crushed red pepper{1/8%tsp}. Cook and stir for ~{4%minutes}, or until browned.

Add @chicken broth{3/4%cup}, @sundried tomatoes{1/2%cup}(drained and cut into strips), and @dry white wine{1/4%cup}. Bring to a boil; reduce heat.

Simmer uncovered for about ~{10%minutes} or until chicken is tender and no longer pink. 

Stir in @whipping cream{1/2%cup} and @parmesan cheese{1/4%cup}(grated); simmer ~{2%minutes} more.

Stir pasta into chicken mixture. Heat through. Serve with additional parmesan cheese if desired.

> Using anything but real parmeggiano reggiano for this recipe is a jailable offense.